WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:05.509
Where do we go after Masters of the Universe:
Revelation Part 1 ended on the mother of all

00:00:05.509 --> 00:00:06.509
cliffhangers?

00:00:06.509 --> 00:00:08.250
What's a He-Man to do without a Sword of Power?

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:10.750
And what's going to happen next if we get
another season?

00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:11.750
Let's dig in.

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:17.700
"Revelation Part 2" kicks off by briefly exploring
Teela's backstory.Teela's mother is revealed

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:21.510
to be none other than the Sorceress of Castle
Grayskull, who couldn't stay to raise her

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:24.880
daughter with Man-At-Arms because of her duty
as the new Sorceress.

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:28.040
She's clearly distraught over the thought
of not being with her daughter, but she paints

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:32.140
a magical protection charm on her which will
activate when she needs it the most.

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:36.390
Meanwhile, with Skeletor wielding the Sword
of Power, he has everything he's ever wanted

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:40.620
and begins turning the Eternian citizens into
a mindless zombie army.

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:45.050
It's this dire situation that forces Prince
Adam to try a radical solution: what happens

00:00:45.050 --> 00:00:49.880
if he says the iconic words he uses to transform
without holding the sword?

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:53.739
He transforms into Savage He-Man, a mindless
brute who has all of the hero's strength and

00:00:53.739 --> 00:00:55.269
none of his brains.

00:00:55.269 --> 00:00:59.079
This is because the power is raw and unrefined
when it doesn't flow through the sword, so

00:00:59.079 --> 00:01:03.769
he doesn't retain his own personality and
is just a being of pure rage ... He's basically

00:01:03.769 --> 00:01:04.770
a blonde Hulk.

00:01:04.770 --> 00:01:09.189
However, the only thing that gets through
to Savage He-Man is his father, King Randor.

00:01:09.189 --> 00:01:13.100
In the time since Adam's death, the King spent
a lot of time wishing he'd told his son that

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:14.100
he loves him.

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:17.150
Now that he's alive again, the King finally
tells him that to his face.

00:01:17.150 --> 00:01:21.030
It's those words that bring Adam out of his
Savage He-Man persona at Point Dread.

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:24.590
"I haven't told you I loved you.

00:01:24.590 --> 00:01:26.659
And I haven't told you I'm proud of you."

00:01:26.659 --> 00:01:30.909
After coming into power, one of Skeletor's
first acts of business is to make Evil-Lyn

00:01:30.909 --> 00:01:34.729
the new sorceress, which she isn't exactly
pleased about because this keeps her locked

00:01:34.729 --> 00:01:36.020
away in Grayskull.

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:39.770
Although Skeletor gives her access to the
entire universe, she's still not happy that

00:01:39.770 --> 00:01:43.119
he keeps using her as a tool, rather than
as an ally.

00:01:43.119 --> 00:01:46.909
It's difficult for Lyn, especially since she's
been with Skeletor most of her life.

00:01:46.909 --> 00:01:50.659
But ultimately Skeletor's own short-sighted
goals make her realize that she can do so

00:01:50.659 --> 00:01:51.659
much better.

00:01:51.659 --> 00:01:55.929
He waxes lyrical about wanting to kill He-Man
once and for all, and it's here she comes

00:01:55.929 --> 00:02:00.119
to the realization that Skeletor has no real
ambitions for the rest of the universe outside

00:02:00.119 --> 00:02:02.310
of his eternal battle with Prince Adam.

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:03.350
"Then what?"

00:02:03.350 --> 00:02:06.490
"What do you mean 'then what?'

00:02:06.490 --> 00:02:09.880
I kill this version of He-Man too."

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:14.032
She even points out how dim-witted Skeletor
really is, as she seduces him to distract

00:02:14.032 --> 00:02:16.840
the villain so she can take the Sword of Power
for herself.

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:20.890
Evil-Lyn takes the chance to transform into
an ethereal, omniscient warrior.

00:02:20.890 --> 00:02:24.950
However, Lyn is forced to see all the universe
at once and makes the decision that she should

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:27.930
use her powers to snuff out every living thing.

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:32.470
One of the most surprising moments in the
series sees Skeletor surrender to the Eternian

00:02:32.470 --> 00:02:35.640
forces, offering to team up with Prince Adam
to stop Evil-Lyn.

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:40.610
Hang on, did the lord of Snake Mountain actually
put the greater good ahead of his own desires

00:02:40.610 --> 00:02:41.610
for once?

00:02:41.610 --> 00:02:42.860
Now that's character development.

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:46.960
Still, the skull-faced baddie is obviously
aware that if Lyn wipes out the universe,

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:51.260
he'll have his own power stripped away from
him -- so it is more about self-preservation

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:52.870
rather than selflessness.

00:02:52.870 --> 00:02:57.180
Unfortunately, even their team-up isn't enough
to simply put a stop to Lyn when she raises

00:02:57.180 --> 00:02:59.530
the Subternian dead as her new army.

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:04.050
A sprawling battle between good and evil rages
on, while Adam and Skeletor try to keep Lyn

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:06.910
distracted long enough to get the Sword of
Power.

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:10.970
If there was any doubt about Adam's pure-heartedness,
it's dispelled here.

00:03:10.970 --> 00:03:14.640
The hero puts his own eternal quarrel with
Skeletor aside, knowing that they need to

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:15.640
work together.

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:20.070
And once he gets his own powers back, he enhances
Skeletor back to his own hulking self too.

00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:23.480
But there's a very specific reason why he
does this.

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:24.800
"But why?"

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:29.450
"Because I want you to know what saving the
universe feels like."

00:03:29.450 --> 00:03:33.900
Teela is understandably reluctant to embrace
her own magical abilities -- largely because

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:37.200
she's still resentful for the fact that her
mother never tried to connect with her all

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:39.300
those years fighting for Grayskull.

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:42.970
That's on top of the fact that if she becomes
the new Sorceress, she'll be tied to the castle

00:03:42.970 --> 00:03:45.370
and will never be allowed to leave.

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:49.790
But she tackles all of her concerns head-on,
even speaking with the ethereal ghost of the

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:51.710
Sorceress about how to make the mantle into
her own.

00:03:51.710 --> 00:03:54.780
She refuses to do it the old isolated way,
explaining:

00:03:54.780 --> 00:03:59.630
"Because holding on to the ones I love only
makes me stronger."

00:03:59.630 --> 00:04:03.780
In short, she's relying on the close bond
she has with her friends to wield the Sorceress'

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:06.030
power in a new way, triumphantly saying,

00:04:06.030 --> 00:04:08.110
“We have the power."

00:04:08.110 --> 00:04:12.820
And sure, she gets into a flashy fight with
Lyn as the two show off their respective abilities

00:04:12.820 --> 00:04:16.782
-- but Teela shows the villain the magnificence
of the universe, even convincing her to give

00:04:16.782 --> 00:04:18.060
up her power.

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:21.010
Ultimately, Lyn just needs someone to get
through to her softer side.

00:04:22.180 --> 00:04:25.760
He-Man and Skeletor should definitely take
a leaf out of Teela and Lyn's book because

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:29.650
they revert back to their typical fisticuffs
while the two sorcerers talk it out.

00:04:29.650 --> 00:04:33.960
But that's all Skeletor wants -- to be, quote,
"locked in an eternal battle."

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:36.480
But He-Man isn't down with that.

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:39.700
"it's not about us."

00:04:39.700 --> 00:04:44.660
It's a simple line, but he's essentially saying
that their ongoing fight means nothing in

00:04:44.660 --> 00:04:46.320
the grand scheme of things.

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:50.520
He-Man hurls the villain into the outer reaches
of space, and all is right in the world — at

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:51.990
least for now.

00:04:51.990 --> 00:04:56.130
Eternia rebuilds as it always does, while
Lyn puts herself into self-exile in a peaceful

00:04:56.130 --> 00:04:58.960
location surrounded by the beauty of life.

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:03.010
But a final intriguing scene sees Skeletor
visit his former acolytes who now worship

00:05:03.010 --> 00:05:04.880
an A.I. called Motherboard.

00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:09.870
This malevolent new entity transforms into
a winged robotic giant, before plunging several

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:13.300
claws into Skeletor and filling him with a
techno-virus.

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:17.271
It doesn't look like it kills him, so this
isn't the last of Skeletor.

00:05:17.271 --> 00:05:21.150
But the robot displays the holographic symbol
of Hordak, Skeletor's old mentor.

00:05:21.150 --> 00:05:25.510
It looks like Eternia has caught the attention
of a vicious new enemy.

